{"skill":{"slug":"nano-banana-pro","displayName":"Nano Banana Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1767651987917,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5701,"sha256":"4ea88f4b0e9577e22fb68111fb2efcacb3f5c034dee3f8f6f8aeabaa96a7988b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/generate_image.py","size":5613,"sha256":"8ecca97db200cab923716173fed18e48ce7e291b1726c4e6ed79fa88302023e8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2028,"sha256":"8e724ebfbbb3bded620d0f7bcbbda1382c5fc815620e26d35946502841a7cae9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013611048,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"42d41782d4c3c790e22e0eb26a444ea386e234cbdd75b9a57a10a55dab6ca98e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/42d41782d4c3c790e22e0eb26a444ea386e234cbdd75b9a57a10a55dab6ca98e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: nano-banana-pro\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe `scripts/generate_image.py` script allows reading arbitrary local files specified via the `--input-image` argument using `PIL.Image.open()`. If the provided path points to a sensitive file (e.g., a screenshot of credentials, or a document containing PII) that PIL can successfully open, its content will be sent to the external Google Gemini API (`gemini-3-pro-image-preview`). While the stated purpose is image editing, this capability presents a significant data exfiltration risk if the agent is prompted to provide paths to sensitive files, even without explicit malicious intent from the skill developer.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159617336},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":30,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789013611048},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This image-generation skill is mostly coherent, but it handles a Gemini API key in ways that can expose the secret and does not clearly warn before sending prompts or images to Google.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to Google, reading an optional local input image, reading GEMINI_API_KEY, and writing the requested output file are proportionate for this image API skill, but users should understand that selected content leaves the local machine.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented uv-run workflow uses inline dependency metadata with minimum-version constraints for google-genai and pillow, so future dependency versions may be resolved at run time without a lockfile.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are generally task-scoped, but they explicitly allow using an API key provided in chat and passing it as a command-line argument, which can expose a sensitive credential in transcripts, process arguments, shell history, or logs.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, background worker, privilege escalation, shell profile modification, memory writing, or hidden installation behavior was found in the inspected artifact files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is to generate and edit images using Google's Gemini image API, and the script does exactly that by sending the prompt and optional input image to the Google client and saving a PNG output.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Prefer setting GEMINI_API_KEY in a protected environment instead of pasting keys into chat or using --api-key, avoid confidential prompts or private images unless Google API upload is acceptable, and consider pinning dependencies or using a lockfile before routine use.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Use of GEMINI_API_KEY and command execution is expected for this API-backed image tool, but the otherwise empty metadata and limited privacy notice reduce transparency.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending prompts and optional input images to Google's API is core to the stated purpose and is not hidden, but the skill lacks a clear user-facing warning about third-party upload of sensitive prompts or images.\n[T08] unexpected: Open-ended uv dependencies are not required by the image-generation purpose and create avoidable supply-chain drift, though no malicious dependency behavior is present in the artifact.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepting and documenting --api-key, especially when the key may be provided in chat, is an avoidable credential-exposure risk and is the main reason this needs review rather than simple approval.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013611048}}}}}